-- title:
--   Branch lengths in the crossing model equal lengths at a node prime
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, a perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke degeneracy maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ at level $N$ and prime $q$, and a place specialisation $P$ built from these; let $R$ be a prolongation tuple for $P$, $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$, and $w$ a place of the level-$N$ modular function field over $k$. Write $B = R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ for the ring of functions in the level-$Nq$ modular function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are integral for both prolongations $R_1,R_2$ and at every place over $w$ and whose Laurent expansion lies in the subfield generated by the constants of $K$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$, and $\mathcal O = A \cap K$ for the coefficient subring. The data are: node coordinates $c = (x,y)$ at $(K,w)$, i.e. $x$ with vanishing first residue and $\mathrm{ord} = 1$ for the second residue at the Frobenius translate $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\cdot w$ and $y$ with vanishing second residue and $w.\mathrm{ord} = 1$ for the first; a nonzero $\varpi \in \mathcal O$; hypotheses that $B$ is local and noetherian with maximal ideal $(\varpi, x, y)$ (the constant $\varpi$ being its image under $R.\mathrm{nodeConst}$), that every $g \in B$ differs from some constant by a non-unit, that $R$ satisfies the value integrality law at $w$ (reductions at places over $w$ of functions integral at $w$ lie in $A$), that $w$ is a supersingular place (rational, affine at $j$ and $j_N$, with supersingular $j$-invariant), that every prime strictly contained in a non-maximal prime of $B$ is $\bot$, and that every element of the field $\mathrm{fieldOver}\ (Nq)\ K$ is a quotient of two elements of $B$; a complete discrete valuation domain $W$ with irreducible $\pi$, an exponent $E \ge 1$, and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $B$ onto the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^{E})$ carrying the constant $\varpi$ to $\mathrm{const}\ \pi$ and $x$ to $U$ times a unit $\alpha_U$; the assumption that $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$ together with an isomorphism $\tau$ of its adic completion onto $W$ sending $\varpi$ to $\pi$ and compatible with $\iota$ on constants; a nonzero prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ containing no nonzero constant; the assumptions that $k$ is algebraically closed, $q \nmid N$, and $R$ satisfies $\mathrm{OrderLawFixed}$; and two order-reading clauses stating that if the first residue of $g$ is nonzero with $w.\mathrm{ord} = n$ then $\iota(g) \equiv \gamma V^{n}$ modulo $(\mathrm{const}\ \pi, U)$ for some unit $\gamma$, and symmetrically that if the second residue is nonzero with order $n$ at $\mathrm{arithFrobC}\cdot w$ then $\iota(g) \equiv \gamma U^{n}$ modulo $(\mathrm{const}\ \pi, V)$. Let $Q$ be a prime of the crossing model that is a minimal prime over the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak q$ under $\iota$ composed with the completion map, with $\mathrm{const}\ \pi \notin Q$. Then for every nonzero $g \in B$ the length over $\mathcal O_{Q}$ of the localisation at $Q$ of $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^{E},\iota(g))$ equals the length over $B_{\mathfrak q}$ of the localisation at $\mathfrak q$ of $B/(g)$.
--
--   This is the statement that each branch $Q$ of the completed crossing model lying over a non-constant prime $\mathfrak q$ of the node ring is analytically unramified over $\mathfrak q$: multiplicities of elements of the node ring are read off unchanged on the branch. It is the termwise refinement of the kernel-class count at a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$, and is used in the determination of the residue orders along the two components and of $\mathrm{ord}(y - \text{constant})$ for the second node coordinate.
